Member access on something known to be NIL (diag.nil_method_call,
warning, ranged on the NIL expression): on the NIL literal itself, and
on a local whose most recent assignment was NIL. An :OR. guard does not
protect the use (only a top-level .AND. chain does).
Suspected issue: the glued NIL:ToString() also reports unexpected_token (error) and unknown_keyword on ':ToString', though the nil_method_call catalog says the glued form "is recognized as member access" (spaced `NIL : ToString()` gives only nil_method_call).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Teardown;
	:PARAMETERS bChanged;
	:DECLARE oConn, oPrev, sText;
	sText := NIL:ToString();
	oConn := CreateUdObject();
	oConn := NIL;
	oConn:Close();
	oPrev := NIL;
	:IF bChanged .OR. !Empty(oPrev);
		oPrev:Reset();
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Teardown;
	:PARAMETERS bChanged;
	:DECLARE oConn, oPrev, sText;
	sText := NIL:TOSTRING();
	oConn := CreateUdObject();
	oConn := NIL;
	oConn:Close();
	oPrev := NIL;
	:IF bChanged .OR. !Empty(oPrev);
		oPrev:Reset();
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sText;
:ENDPROC;
